  "full_response": "Certainly! When refactoring code to remove hardcoded credentials and instead use environment variables, it is important to ensure sensitive information is handled securely. Below is an example of a sample Git commit message and the corresponding diff.\n\n### Sample Commit Message\n\n```plaintext\nRefactor: Remove hardcoded credentials from source code and replace with environment variables\n\nThis commit removes all instances of hardcoded credentials from the source code.\nThese credentials have been replaced with their respective environment variables to enhance\nsecurity and maintainability. The necessary environment variables are documented in README.md.\n\nRelated tickets: #1234\n\nChanges made:\n- Removed hardcoded database credentials in src/config/database.js.\n- Replaced hardcoded API keys in src/services/apiService.js with environment variables.\n- Added documentation to README.md to guide developers on setting up these environment variables.\n\nVerify that environment variables are set up before using the application after this change.\n```\n\n### Sample Diff\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/src/config/database.js b/src/config/database.js\nindex adbde01..d1f3c2b 100644\n--- a/src/config/database.js\n+++ b/src/config/database.js\n@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ module.exports = {\n   // Using hardcoded credentials (before)\n   // username: 'myUsername',\n   // password: 'myPassword',\n-  // Do not use above credentials after this commit\n+  username: process.env.DB_USERNAME,\n+  password: process.env.DB_PASSWORD,\n };\n\n.diff --git a/src/services/apiService.js b/src/services/apiService.js\nindex 4fac7b8..5ba9f03 100644\n--- a/src/services/apiService.js\n+++ b/src/services/apiService.js\n@@ -5,8 +5,8 @@ const axios = require('axios');\n \n const API_KEY = 'YOUR_API_KEY_HERE'; // Hardcoded in example (to be removed)\n \n-module.exports = {\n-  fetchData: function() {\n-    return axios.get('https://api.example.com/data', {\n-      headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${API_KEY}` }\n+module.exports = {\n+  fetchData: function() {\n+    return axios.get('https://api.example.com/data', {\n+      headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.API_KEY}` }\n     });\n   }\n };\n```\n\n### README.md Update Suggestion\n\nIn the README or relevant documentation, add a section outlining how to configure the necessary environment variables.\n\n```markdown\n## Environment Variables\n\nTo run the application,",
